:5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.13918608426656998,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":95.7,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02419393340102617,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":38.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03445518118098434,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":6.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.020794446448698444,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":65.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.28174,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.4,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":40.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Byline Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Byline Bank that provides various banking products and services for small and medium sized businesses, commercial real estate and financial sponsors, and consumers in the United States. It offers various retail deposit products, including non-interest-bearing accounts, money market demand accounts, savings accounts, interest-bearing checking accounts, and time deposits; ATM and debit cards; and online, mobile, and text banking services, as well as commercial deposits. The company also provides term loans, revolving lines of credit, and construction financing services; senior secured financing solutions to private equity backed lower middle market companies; small business administration and the United States department of agriculture loans; and treasury management products and services, such as treasury services, information reporting, fraud management, cash collection, and interest rate derivative products. In addition, it offers financing solutions for equipment vendors and their end users; syndication services; and investment, trust, and wealth management services, including fiduciary and executor services, financial planning solutions, investment advisory services, and private banking services for foundations and endowments, and high net worth individuals. The company was formerly known as Metropolitan Bank Group, Inc. and changed its name to Byline Bancorp, Inc. in 2015. Byline Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1914 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Roberto R. Herencia | Executive Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $438K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $134K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Byline Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.7B market cap on $446M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $136M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.08\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 28% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $24.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-24892013.91},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 38% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered